bhū́rṇi, a. [von bhur], 1〉 eifrig, eifervoll von Menschen und Göttern; 2〉 gierig; 3〉 feurig, wild, kräftig.<BR>-is 2〉 tákvā {66,2}; paśús {603,2}.<BR>-im 1〉 agním {237,5}. — 3〉 mṛgám {621,20}; áśvam {637,15}.<BR>-aye 1〉 devā́ya {602,7}. — 3〉 mádāya {763,4}.<BR>-ayas 1〉 náras {645,15}; {708,1}; ásya spáśas^1 {785,4}; (erg. náras) {727,3}. — 3〉 kétās {55,7}; sómās {729,1}; gā́vas {753,1}.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Unknown, Jim Funderburk on 20180518. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/Cologne/issues/223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=GRA&page=0954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=gra" target="_blank">Correction</a>

