(harmyá), harmiá, a., n. [von 2. ghar, also für *gharmiá, was in gharmieṣṭhā neben harmieṣṭhā mit harmiá wechselt], ursprünglich „Feuerstätte, Herd“; daher 1〉 n., Haus, Wohnstätte; 2〉 n., Hausgenossenschaft, Familie; 3〉 Kerker.<BR>-ám 2〉 {571,6} (idám).<BR>-ásya 1〉 viśas {121,1}. — 2〉 sakṣáṇim {783,4}; {790,3}.<BR>-é 1〉 {625,23}; {940,10}. — 3〉 yúyutsantam 〰 dhā́s {386,5}.<BR>-ā́ 1〉 neben bhúvanāni {166,4}.<BR>-ébhyas [Ab.] 1〉 ádhi {592,2}.<BR>-éṣu 1〉 {872,3} (jātás agnís); {899,10}.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=GRA&page=1651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=gra" target="_blank">Correction</a>

